					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12103420#post-4285306</guid>
				<title>Re: Some inaccuracies regarding wws lore</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12103420/critter-profile:arorangi#post-4285306</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 19 Jun 2019 12:04:34 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>margssentif</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3861605</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Ok, thanks.</p> <p>I've shuffled the dates around to concord with the canon.<br /> As for the Boring Agreement: Darkstuff, along with other critters, didn't think it would be much of a stretch for the Foundation to give something that required large amounts of care to responsible and Foundation-supervised people who could provide that care.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
					<item>
				<guid>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12103420#post-4285286</guid>
				<title>Some inaccuracies regarding wws lore</title>
				<link>http://www.scpwiki.com/forum/t-12103420/critter-profile:arorangi#post-4285286</link>
				<description></description>
				<pubDate>Wed, 19 Jun 2019 11:37:56 +0000</pubDate>
				<wikidot:authorName>Uncle Nicolini</wikidot:authorName>				<wikidot:authorUserId>3487700</wikidot:authorUserId>				<content:encoded>
					<![CDATA[
						 <p>Wws wasn't under Foundation supervision until 2008.<br /> Additionally, the Boring Agreemenr only lets them keep and take care of animals found within the Boring Nexus, meaning that they wouldn't be given an animal found by the Foundation elsewhere.</p> <p>That aside, not bad.</p> 
				 	]]>
				</content:encoded>							</item>
